IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Rates Act 1986 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- at what rates my taxable income is taxed: the s 3 definitions
-- (tax-free threshold, prescribed non-resident, resident taxpayer, ordinary taxable income, the superannuation and employment
-- termination remainders, non-profit company), s 3A (working holiday makers), s 12(1), Schedule 7 Parts I, II and III (the
-- resident, non-resident and working holiday maker tables, clause 2 of Parts I and II (a special income component) and clause
-- 4), ss 16, 18 and 20(1) (the part-year residency period and the pro-rated tax-free threshold),
-- and for my company s 23(2) and (6), s 23AA (base rate entity) and s 23AB (base rate entity passive income).
--
-- SEAT: the taxpayer -- the individual whose taxable income is taxed, and (Daniel's life) the founder asking at what rate his
-- company is taxed. Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 66, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 50, 2026 (Register id
-- C2026C00300), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.txt. No other instrument sets these numbers: the rates
-- are in the Act's own text, amended each Budget. The text deposit drops every formula that was set as an image ("in accordance
-- with the following formula:" is followed by nothing). They are transcribed by hand from the Word rendering of the same
-- compilation in ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.formulas.md (2026-10-21); this encoding uses s 20(1) and Schedule 7
-- Parts I and II clause 2.
--
-- DATED ARM FOR 2023-24 (REQ-0056, 22 October 2026). Compilation No. 62, compilation date 1 April 2024, includes amendments up
-- to Act No. 3, 2024 (Register id C2024C00132), the compilation in force at the end of the 2023-24 year of income, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A03348.2024-04-01.txt (formulas in C2004A03348.2024-04-01.formulas.md: the
-- same as Compilation No. 66's). Its Schedule 7 Parts I, II and III each have a table "for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or
-- 2023-24 year of income"; this encoding uses those tables for 2023-24 only. Every other provision encoded here reads the same
-- in both compilations (s 3 "tax-free threshold means $18,200"; s 20(1)'s $4,736; Schedule 7 clauses 2 and 4), except s 16
-- "eligible pensioner" (c), which in Compilation No. 62 also leaves out Part 3.15A of the Social Security Act 1991 -- an
-- eligible pensioner is asked as a fact, so only the question's wording changes.
--
-- YEARS THE DEPOSITED TEXT COVERS. In Compilation No. 66, Schedule 7 Part I has three resident tables: "for the 2024-25 or
-- 2025-26 year of income", "for the 2026-27 year of income" and "for the 2027-28 year of income or a later year of income".
-- Part II (non-residents) and Part III (working holiday makers) each have one table, "for the 2024-25 year of income or a later
-- year of income". 2023-24 is answered from Compilation No. 62 (above). For the 2022-23 year of income and earlier, every answer
-- here is `Not in the deposited text`: Compilation No. 62's tables name those years too, but it is not the compilation that was
-- in force for them.
--
-- A year of income is named by the calendar year in which it begins: 2024 is the 2024-25 year of income.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Schedule 7 clause 3 (a special income component where Division 16 of the 1936 Act or Division 392 of the 1997
-- Act applies -- it needs the "average income" of s 392-45), a special income component together with a superannuation or
-- employment termination remainder (s 3 "special income component" (b)) or with working holiday taxable income (clause 4(c)):
-- each gets `Not covered by this encoding`; s 12(2)-(13), 12AA, 12A (notional rates, trustees, minimum tax capital gains, primary producers); ss 13-15 (Division 6AA
-- minors' income); s 20(1A)-(3) (trustees); Schedules 8 to 12; s 23(3)-(5), (7), 23A and ss 25-30 (RSA providers, PDFs,
-- recognised medium credit unions, life insurers, trusts, super funds, ADFs, no-TFN contributions, sovereign entities) -- a
-- company of those kinds gets `Not covered by this encoding`; ss 1, 2, 4, 5, 21 (machinery). Rounding to whole dollars is not
-- modelled. Tax offsets (the low income tax offset), the Medicare levy and HELP repayments are in other Acts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual to whom the law is applied, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Rates Act 1986 -- rates`

§§ `Answers and helpers`

-- Every money or rate answer is either an amount, or says plainly that the deposited compilation has no rule for the case, or
-- that the case is one this encoding leaves out.
DECLARE Answer IS ONE OF
    Amount HAS `value` IS A NUMBER
    `Not in the deposited text`
    `Not covered by this encoding`

GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER, `from` IS A NUMBER, `width` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the slice` MEANS
    IF `amount` AT MOST `from` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `amount` MINUS `from` GREATER THAN `width` THEN `width` ELSE `amount` MINUS `from`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- A width large enough to stand for "exceeds $190,000" with no upper limit.
`no upper limit` MEANS 1000000000000

§§ `s 3 -- the tax-free threshold`

-- s 3(1): "tax-free threshold means $18,200." (Gloss: the part of a resident's ordinary taxable income taxed at nil.)
@export What is the tax-free threshold in the deposited text, in dollars (s 3)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the tax-free threshold` IS 18200

§§ `Schedule 7 -- which table applies to my year`

-- Schedule 7 Part I clause 1(b): "for each part of the ordinary taxable income specified in the table applicable to the year of
-- income -- the rate applicable under that table". The tables, as data:
--   2023-24 (Compilation No. 62, "for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of income"): item 1 "exceeds the tax-free
--     threshold but does not exceed $45,000" 19%; item 2 "exceeds $45,000 but does not exceed $120,000" 32.5%; item 3 "exceeds
--     $120,000 but does not exceed $180,000" 37%; item 4 "exceeds $180,000" 45%.
--   2024-25 or 2025-26: item 1 "exceeds the tax-free threshold but does not exceed $45,000" 16%; item 2 "exceeds $45,000 but does
--     not exceed $135,000" 30%; item 3 "exceeds $135,000 but does not exceed $190,000" 37%; item 4 "exceeds $190,000" 45%.
--   2026-27: 15%, 30%, 37%, 45%.
--   2027-28 or a later year: 14%, 30%, 37%, 45%.
DECLARE `Resident table` IS ONE OF
    `the table for 2023-24`
    `the table for 2024-25 or 2025-26`
    `the table for 2026-27`
    `the table for 2027-28 or a later year`
    `no table in the deposited text`

-- The rate of each item, and the dollar figure at which items 1, 2 and 3 stop ("does not exceed $45,000", "$135,000",
-- "$190,000" from 2024-25; "$45,000", "$120,000", "$180,000" in 2023-24).
DECLARE `Table rates` HAS
    `item 1 rate` IS A NUMBER
    `item 2 rate` IS A NUMBER
    `item 3 rate` IS A NUMBER
    `item 4 rate` IS A NUMBER
    `item 1 top` IS A NUMBER
    `item 2 top` IS A NUMBER
    `item 3 top` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Resident table`
`the resident table for` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `year` LESS THAN 2023 THEN `no table in the deposited text`
        IF `year` EQUALS 2023    THEN `the table for 2023-24`
        IF `year` AT MOST 2025   THEN `the table for 2024-25 or 2025-26`
        IF `year` EQUALS 2026    THEN `the table for 2026-27`
        OTHERWISE `the table for 2027-28 or a later year`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Resident table`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Table rates`
`the rates in` MEANS
    CONSIDER `t`
    WHEN `the table for 2023-24`                THEN JUST (`Table rates` 19 32.5 37 45 45000 120000 180000)
    WHEN `the table for 2024-25 or 2025-26`     THEN JUST (`Table rates` 16 30 37 45 45000 135000 190000)
    WHEN `the table for 2026-27`                THEN JUST (`Table rates` 15 30 37 45 45000 135000 190000)
    WHEN `the table for 2027-28 or a later year` THEN JUST (`Table rates` 14 30 37 45 45000 135000 190000)
    WHEN `no table in the deposited text`       THEN NOTHING

@export Does the deposited text give income tax rates for my year of income (Schedule 7)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2024 for 2024-25)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the deposited text give rates for my year` IF
    CONSIDER `the resident table for` `year`
    WHEN `no table in the deposited text` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Which Schedule 7 Part I table applies to my year of income?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2024 for 2024-25)
GIVETH A `Resident table`
DECIDE `Which resident table applies to my year` IS `the resident table for` `year`

§§ `s 3 -- prescribed non-resident, resident taxpayer`

-- s 3(1): "prescribed non-resident ... means a person who, at all times during the year of income, is a non-resident, not being
-- a person to whom, at any time during the year of income, compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit is payable under:
-- (a) the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; (b) subsection 4(6) of the Veterans' Entitlements (Transitional Provisions and
-- Consequential Amendments) Act 1986; or (ba) the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004; or (c) the Social Security
-- Act 1991; being compensation or a pension, allowance or benefit in respect of which the person is liable to be assessed and to
-- pay income tax in Australia." "resident taxpayer ... means a taxpayer who is not a prescribed non-resident".
-- "Non-resident" is a borrowed term (the Assessment Act) and is asked as a fact.
@export Am I a resident taxpayer for the rates of income tax (s 3)?
GIVEN `a non-resident at all times during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were a non-resident of Australia for tax purposes for the whole year of income
      `paid a taxable veterans', military compensation or social security payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time in the year you were paid a pension, allowance, benefit or compensation under the Veterans' Entitlements Act, the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act or the Social Security Act on which you are liable to Australian income tax
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a resident taxpayer` IF
    NOT (    `a non-resident at all times during the year`
         AND (NOT `paid a taxable veterans', military compensation or social security payment`))

§§ `s 3A -- working holiday makers`

-- s 3A(1): "An individual is a working holiday maker at a particular time if the individual holds at that time: (a) a Subclass
-- 417 (Working Holiday) visa; or (b) a Subclass 462 (Work and Holiday) visa; or (c) a bridging visa permitting the individual to
-- work in Australia if: (i) the bridging visa was granted ... in relation to an application for a visa of a kind described in
-- paragraph (a) or (b); and (ii) the Minister ... is still to make a decision in relation to the application; and (iii) the most
-- recent visa, other than a bridging visa, granted ... was a visa of a kind described in paragraph (a) or (b); or (d) a COVID-19
-- pandemic event 408 visa".
DECLARE Visa IS ONE OF
    `a Subclass 417 Working Holiday visa`
    `a Subclass 462 Work and Holiday visa`
    `a work bridging visa awaiting a 417 or 462 decision, after a 417 or 462`
    `a COVID-19 pandemic event 408 visa`
    `another visa, or none`

@export Was I a working holiday maker in the year of income (s 3A(1))?
GIVEN `visa` IS A Visa @desc The visa you held at some time during the year (choose a working holiday kind if you held one at any time)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I a working holiday maker` IF
    CONSIDER `visa`
    WHEN `another visa, or none` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 3A(2): "working holiday taxable income ... is the individual's assessable income for the year of income derived: (a) from
-- sources in Australia; and (b) while the individual is a working holiday maker; less so much of any amount the individual can
-- deduct for the year of income as relates to that assessable income." (3): it "does not include any superannuation remainder,
-- or employment termination remainder". The two amounts are facts the taxpayer states, remainders already left out.
@export What is my working holiday taxable income (s 3A(2), (3))?
GIVEN `Australian-source income earned while a working holiday maker` IS A NUMBER @desc Your assessable income from sources in Australia derived while you held a working holiday visa, leaving out any superannuation or employment termination remainder, in dollars
      `deductions relating to it` IS A NUMBER @desc The deductions you can claim that relate to that income, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my working holiday taxable income` IS
    `the greater of` (`Australian-source income earned while a working holiday maker` MINUS `deductions relating to it`) 0

§§ `ss 16, 18, 20(1) -- part-year residency and the pro-rated threshold`

-- s 18(1): part-year residency periods arise where the person "ceased to be a resident" during a month, "commenced to be a
-- resident during a month", or both, in the year of income. s 18(2): "A period shall not be taken to be a part-year residency
-- period ... if: (a) the person is an eligible pensioner in relation to the year of income; or (b) the period is the whole of the
-- year of income." s 16: an "eligible pensioner" is paid a taxable payment under the Veterans' Entitlements Act, the MRCA, or "a
-- provision of the Social Security Act 1991 other than Part 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15" (asked as a fact).
@export Is there a part-year residency period for me, so that my tax-free threshold is pro-rated (ss 18, 20)?
GIVEN `became or ceased to be a resident during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you started or stopped being an Australian resident part-way through the year of income
      `an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time in the year you were paid a taxable veterans', military compensation or social security payment (other than under Parts 2.11, 2.12 or 2.15 of the Social Security Act, and for 2023-24 Part 3.15A)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is there a part-year residency period for me` IF
    `became or ceased to be a resident during the year` AND (NOT `an eligible pensioner`)

-- s 20(1): with one or more part-year residency periods, the Schedule 7 Part I reference to the tax-free threshold is read "as if
-- [it] were a reference to the amount calculated in accordance with the following formula" -- transcribed in
-- C2004A03348.formulas.md from the authorised rendering:
--     (The tax-free threshold - $4,736)
--       + ($4,736 x Number of months in the year of income during which there is a part-year residency period
--                   in relation to the person and the year of income / 12)
-- (Gloss: $13,464 for any part-year resident, plus $394.67 for each month of residence. s 18(1) counts whole months: the
-- period runs from the beginning of the month of arrival, or to the end of the month of departure.)
@export What is my pro-rated tax-free threshold, in dollars, if I was a resident for only part of the year (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of months of the year of income in your part-year residency period (s 18: from the start of the month you became a resident, or to the end of the month you stopped)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my pro-rated tax-free threshold` IS
    (`What is the tax-free threshold` MINUS 4736) PLUS 4736 TIMES `months` DIVIDED BY 12

-- A non-resident taxpayer gets no threshold: the Part II table starts at $0.
@export What tax-free threshold do I get, in dollars (s 3; s 20(1); Schedule 7 Parts I and II)?
GIVEN `a resident taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a resident taxpayer for the rates (see the s 3 question)
      `became or ceased to be a resident during the year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you started or stopped being a resident part-way through the year
      `an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an eligible pensioner in the year (s 16)
      `months in a part-year residency period` IS A NUMBER @desc If you started or stopped being a resident in the year, the number of months of the year in your part-year residency period (s 18)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What tax-free threshold do I get` IS
    IF NOT `a resident taxpayer` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `Is there a part-year residency period for me` `became or ceased to be a resident during the year` `an eligible pensioner`
         THEN `What is my pro-rated tax-free threshold` `months in a part-year residency period`
         ELSE `What is the tax-free threshold`

§§ `s 3 -- ordinary taxable income`

-- s 3(1): "ordinary taxable income means the taxable income, reduced by the superannuation remainder of the taxable income and
-- by the employment termination remainder of the taxable income." The remainders (Gloss: super and termination payments
-- included under a "maximum tax rate provision" in Divisions 301 and 82 of the 1997 Act that carry no tax offset) are facts.
GIVEN `taxable income` IS A NUMBER, `superannuation remainder` IS A NUMBER, `employment termination remainder` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ordinary taxable income` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`taxable income` MINUS `superannuation remainder` MINUS `employment termination remainder`) 0

§§ `Schedule 7 Parts I, II and III -- the tables as sums of bands`

-- Part I: the resident table for the year, from the threshold that applies.
GIVEN `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `r` IS A `Table rates`, `upto` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the resident table tax up to` MEANS
        `the slice` `upto` `threshold` (`the greater of` (`r`'s `item 1 top` MINUS `threshold`) 0) TIMES `r`'s `item 1 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`r`'s `item 1 top`) (`r`'s `item 2 top` MINUS `r`'s `item 1 top`) TIMES `r`'s `item 2 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`r`'s `item 2 top`) (`r`'s `item 3 top` MINUS `r`'s `item 2 top`) TIMES `r`'s `item 3 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`r`'s `item 3 top`) `no upper limit` TIMES `r`'s `item 4 rate` DIVIDED BY 100

-- Part II, one table "for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income": item 1 "does not exceed $135,000 -- The second
-- resident personal tax rate"; item 2 "exceeds $135,000 but does not exceed $190,000 -- The third resident personal tax rate";
-- item 3 "exceeds $190,000 -- 45%". s 3: the second and third resident personal tax rates are items 2 and 3 of the Part I table
-- "applicable to the year of income". No tax-free threshold.
-- 2023-24 (Compilation No. 62), "Tax rates for non-resident taxpayers for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of
-- income": item 1 "does not exceed $120,000 -- The second resident personal tax rate" (32.5%); item 2 "exceeds $120,000 but does
-- not exceed $180,000 -- 37%"; item 3 "exceeds $180,000 -- 45%". Its item 2 is a plain 37%, which is also that year's third
-- resident personal tax rate, so one rule serves both years; the band edges are the year's Part I item 2 and 3 tops.
GIVEN `r` IS A `Table rates`, `upto` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-resident table tax up to` MEANS
        `the slice` `upto` 0 (`r`'s `item 2 top`) TIMES `r`'s `item 2 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`r`'s `item 2 top`) (`r`'s `item 3 top` MINUS `r`'s `item 2 top`) TIMES `r`'s `item 3 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`r`'s `item 3 top`) `no upper limit` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100

-- Part III, "Tax rates for working holiday makers for the 2024-25 year of income or a later year of income": "does not exceed
-- $45,000 -- 15%"; "exceeds $45,000 but does not exceed $135,000 -- 30%"; "exceeds $135,000 but does not exceed $190,000 --
-- 37%"; "exceeds $190,000 -- 45%".
-- 2023-24 (Compilation No. 62), "Tax rates for working holiday makers for the 2020-21, 2021-22, 2022-23 or 2023-24 year of
-- income": "does not exceed $45,000 -- 15%"; "exceeds $45,000 but does not exceed $120,000 -- 32.5%"; "exceeds $120,000 but does
-- not exceed $180,000 -- 37%"; "exceeds $180,000 -- 45%". Each Part III table is held as a `Table rates` whose item 1 starts at $0.
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Table rates`
`the working holiday table for` MEANS
    IF `year` EQUALS 2023 THEN `Table rates` 15 32.5 37 45 45000 120000 180000
    ELSE `Table rates` 15 30 37 45 45000 135000 190000

GIVEN `w` IS A `Table rates`, `upto` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the working holiday table tax up to` MEANS
        `the slice` `upto` 0 (`w`'s `item 1 top`) TIMES `w`'s `item 1 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`w`'s `item 1 top`) (`w`'s `item 2 top` MINUS `w`'s `item 1 top`) TIMES `w`'s `item 2 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`w`'s `item 2 top`) (`w`'s `item 3 top` MINUS `w`'s `item 2 top`) TIMES `w`'s `item 3 rate` DIVIDED BY 100
    PLUS `the slice` `upto` (`w`'s `item 3 top`) `no upper limit` TIMES `w`'s `item 4 rate` DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `Schedule 7 -- my tax at the general rates`

-- The facts one individual could state about one year of income.
DECLARE Taxpayer HAS
    `year of income begins` IS A NUMBER
    `a non-resident at all times during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid a taxable veterans', military compensation or social security payment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `became or ceased to be a resident during the year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an eligible pensioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months in a part-year residency period` IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `superannuation remainder` IS A NUMBER
    `employment termination remainder` IS A NUMBER
    `abnormal income amount` IS A NUMBER
    `Division 16 of the 1936 Act or Division 392 of the 1997 Act applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `visa held during the year` IS A Visa
    `Australian-source income earned while a working holiday maker` IS A NUMBER
    `deductions relating to it` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`p is a resident taxpayer` MEANS
    `Am I a resident taxpayer` (`p`'s `a non-resident at all times during the year`)
                               (`p`'s `paid a taxable veterans', military compensation or social security payment`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's working holiday taxable income` MEANS
    IF `Was I a working holiday maker` (`p`'s `visa held during the year`)
    THEN `What is my working holiday taxable income` (`p`'s `Australian-source income earned while a working holiday maker`)
                                                    (`p`'s `deductions relating to it`)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's ordinary taxable income` MEANS
    `the ordinary taxable income` (`p`'s `taxable income`) (`p`'s `superannuation remainder`) (`p`'s `employment termination remainder`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's threshold` MEANS
    `What tax-free threshold do I get` (`p is a resident taxpayer` `p`)
                                       (`p`'s `became or ceased to be a resident during the year`)
                                       (`p`'s `an eligible pensioner`)
                                       (`p`'s `months in a part-year residency period`)

-- Clause 4 (Parts I and II alike): "(a) count the taxpayer's working holiday taxable income ... as the first parts (starting from
-- $0) of the taxpayer's ordinary taxable income for the purposes of the table in clause 1 ...; and (b) do not apply the rates in
-- that table to that working holiday taxable income". Because each table is a sum of bands, the clause 1 tax on the parts from w
-- to x is the table tax up to x less the table tax up to w.
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer, `r` IS A `Table rates`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the clause 1 table tax above working holiday income` MEANS
    IF `p is a resident taxpayer` `p`
    THEN     `the resident table tax up to` (`p's threshold` `p`) `r` (`p's ordinary taxable income` `p`)
       MINUS `the resident table tax up to` (`p's threshold` `p`) `r` (`p's working holiday taxable income` `p`)
    ELSE     `the non-resident table tax up to` `r` (`p's ordinary taxable income` `p`)
       MINUS `the non-resident table tax up to` `r` (`p's working holiday taxable income` `p`)

-- Clause 1: "(a) 45% for the superannuation remainder (if any) of the taxable income; (aa) 45% for the employment termination
-- remainder (if any) of the taxable income; (b) for each part of the ordinary taxable income specified in the table applicable to
-- the year of income -- the rate applicable under that table." Part III clause 1: working holiday taxable income at the Part III
-- rates.
--
-- Clause 2 (Parts I and II alike), where the taxable income "consists of or includes a special income component" and neither
-- Division 16 of the 1936 Act nor Division 392 of the 1997 Act applies: "the rate of tax for every $1 of the taxable income is
-- the amount ascertained in accordance with the formula" -- transcribed in C2004A03348.formulas.md: (A + B) / C, where "A is the
-- amount of tax that would be payable by the taxpayer under clause 1 on a taxable income equal to the reduced taxable income;
-- B is 5 times the difference between: (c) the amount of tax ... under clause 1 on a taxable income equal to the sum of: (i) the
-- reduced taxable income; and (ii) 20% of the special income component ...; and (d) the amount of tax ... under clause 1 on a
-- taxable income equal to the reduced taxable income; and C is the number of whole dollars in the taxable income." (Gloss: the
-- abnormal part is taxed at five times the tax on a fifth of it, stacked on the rest. The rate times the taxable income is
-- A + B, since C is the taxable income in whole dollars; rounding is not modelled.) s 3: "special income component" (a) is "so
-- much of the taxable income as does not exceed the abnormal income amount"; "reduced taxable income means the part (if any) of
-- the taxable income other than the special income component". The abnormal income amount (1997 Act Division 405) is asked.
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer, `r` IS A `Table rates`, `x` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's clause 1 tax on` MEANS
    IF `p is a resident taxpayer` `p`
    THEN `the resident table tax up to` (`p's threshold` `p`) `r` `x`
    ELSE `the non-resident table tax up to` `r` `x`

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's special income component` MEANS `the lesser of` (`p`'s `taxable income`) (`p`'s `abnormal income amount`)

GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer, `r` IS A `Table rates`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`p's clause 2 tax` MEANS
    `p's clause 1 tax on` `p` `r` (`p`'s `taxable income` MINUS `p's special income component` `p`)
    PLUS 5 TIMES (    `p's clause 1 tax on` `p` `r` (`p`'s `taxable income` MINUS `p's special income component` `p`
                                                     PLUS 20 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `p's special income component` `p`)
                  MINUS `p's clause 1 tax on` `p` `r` (`p`'s `taxable income` MINUS `p's special income component` `p`))

@export How much income tax is payable on my taxable income before offsets, at the general rates (s 12(1); Schedule 7)?
GIVEN `p` IS A Taxpayer @desc Your facts for the year of income
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much tax is on my taxable income` IS
    CONSIDER `the rates in` (`the resident table for` (`p`'s `year of income begins`))
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Not in the deposited text`
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN
        IF `p`'s `abnormal income amount` GREATER THAN 0 AND `p`'s `taxable income` GREATER THAN 0
        THEN IF    `p`'s `Division 16 of the 1936 Act or Division 392 of the 1997 Act applies to me`
                OR `p`'s `superannuation remainder` GREATER THAN 0
                OR `p`'s `employment termination remainder` GREATER THAN 0
                OR `p's working holiday taxable income` `p` GREATER THAN 0
             THEN `Not covered by this encoding`
             ELSE Amount (`p's clause 2 tax` `p` `r`)
        ELSE Amount (    `p`'s `superannuation remainder` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100
                    PLUS `p`'s `employment termination remainder` TIMES 45 DIVIDED BY 100
                    PLUS `the working holiday table tax up to` (`the working holiday table for` (`p`'s `year of income begins`))
                                                               (`p's working holiday taxable income` `p`)
                    PLUS `the clause 1 table tax above working holiday income` `p` `r`)

-- The common case, asked with three facts: a taxpayer for the whole year, no remainders, no working holiday income, no
-- abnormal income.
@export How much income tax is payable on my taxable income before offsets, if I am a resident or a non-resident all year with no super, termination or working holiday income (Schedule 7 Parts I and II)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2024 for 2024-25)
      `a resident taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a resident taxpayer for the rates
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable income for the year, in dollars
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much tax is on my income, simply` IS
    `How much tax is on my taxable income`
        (Taxpayer `year` (NOT `a resident taxpayer`) FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `taxable income` 0 0 0 FALSE `another visa, or none` 0 0)

-- The marginal rate: the rate the table applies to the part of ordinary taxable income that holds the last dollar.
@export At what rate is the top part of my taxable income taxed, in percent (Schedule 7 Parts I and II)?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which your year of income begins (2024 for 2024-25)
      `a resident taxpayer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a resident taxpayer for the rates
      `taxable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary taxable income for the year, in dollars
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `What is my marginal rate` IS
    CONSIDER `the rates in` (`the resident table for` `year`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `Not in the deposited text`
    WHEN JUST `r` THEN
        Amount (BRANCH
                    IF `taxable income` GREATER THAN `r`'s `item 3 top` THEN `r`'s `item 4 rate`
                    IF `taxable income` GREATER THAN `r`'s `item 2 top` THEN `r`'s `item 3 rate`
                    IF `taxable income` GREATER THAN `r`'s `item 1 top` THEN `r`'s `item 2 rate`
                    IF NOT `a resident taxpayer`            THEN `r`'s `item 2 rate`
                    IF `taxable income` GREATER THAN `What is the tax-free threshold` THEN `r`'s `item 1 rate`
                    OTHERWISE 0)

§§ `s 3 -- non-profit company; s 23AB -- base rate entity passive income`

-- s 3(1): "non-profit company means: (a) a company that is not carried on for the purposes of profit or gain to its individual
-- members and is, by the terms of the company's constituent document, prohibited from making any distribution, whether in
-- money, property or otherwise, to its members; or (b) a friendly society dispensary."
-- s 23AB(1): "Base rate entity passive income is assessable income that is any of the following: (a) a distribution ... by a
-- corporate tax entity ..., other than a non-portfolio dividend ...; (b) an amount of a franking credit ... on such a
-- distribution; (c) a non-share dividend ...; (d) interest (or a payment in the nature of interest), royalties and rent; (e) a
-- gain on a qualifying security ...; (f) a net capital gain ...; (g) an amount included in the assessable income of a partner ...
-- or of a beneficiary ... to the extent that [it] is referable ... to another amount that is base rate entity passive income".
-- s 23AB(2)(a): interest is not interest for (1)(d) if the entity is a financial institution, a registered finance entity, an
-- Australian credit licensee or representative, a securities financial services licensee or representative, or a specified
-- kind; (b) nor "to the extent that it is a return on an equity interest in a company". The borrowed terms are facts.
DECLARE `Company kind` IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary company`
    `an RSA provider, PDF, life insurance company, credit union or trustee`

DECLARE Company HAS
    `kind` IS A `Company kind`
    `assessable income` IS A NUMBER
    `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
    `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER
    `distributions other than non-portfolio dividends` IS A NUMBER
    `franking credits on them` IS A NUMBER
    `non-share dividends` IS A NUMBER
    `interest` IS A NUMBER
    `interest that is a return on an equity interest` IS A NUMBER
    `a lender of the kind in s 23AB(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `royalties and rent` IS A NUMBER
    `gains on qualifying securities` IS A NUMBER
    `net capital gain` IS A NUMBER
    `passive amounts through partnerships or trusts` IS A NUMBER
    `not carried on for the profit of its members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `constitution prohibits distributions to members` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a friendly society dispensary` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest counted as passive` MEANS
    IF `c`'s `a lender of the kind in s 23AB(2)(a)` THEN 0
    ELSE `the greater of` (`c`'s `interest` MINUS `c`'s `interest that is a return on an equity interest`) 0

@export How much of my company's assessable income is base rate entity passive income (s 23AB)?
GIVEN `c` IS A Company @desc Your company's facts for the year of income
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of my company's income is passive` IS
        `c`'s `distributions other than non-portfolio dividends`
    PLUS `c`'s `franking credits on them`
    PLUS `c`'s `non-share dividends`
    PLUS `the interest counted as passive` `c`
    PLUS `c`'s `royalties and rent`
    PLUS `c`'s `gains on qualifying securities`
    PLUS `c`'s `net capital gain`
    PLUS `c`'s `passive amounts through partnerships or trusts`

@export Is my company a non-profit company (s 3)?
GIVEN `c` IS A Company @desc Your company's facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my company a non-profit company` IF
        (`c`'s `not carried on for the profit of its members` AND `c`'s `constitution prohibits distributions to members`)
    OR `c`'s `a friendly society dispensary`

§§ `s 23AA -- base rate entity`

-- "An entity is a base rate entity for a year of income if: (a) no more than 80% of its assessable income for the year of
-- income is base rate entity passive income; and (b) its aggregated turnover (within the meaning of the Income Tax Assessment
-- Act 1997) for the year of income, worked out as at the end of that year, is less than $50 million."
@export Is my company a base rate entity for the year of income (s 23AA)?
GIVEN `c` IS A Company @desc Your company's facts for the year of income
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my company a base rate entity` IF
        `How much of my company's income is passive` `c` AT MOST `c`'s `assessable income` TIMES 80 DIVIDED BY 100
    AND `c`'s `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 50000000

§§ `s 23(2) -- my company's rate`

-- s 23(1): "The rates of tax payable by a company, other than a company in the capacity of a trustee, are as set out in the
-- following provisions". (2): "The rate of tax in respect of the taxable income of a company is: (a) if the company is a base
-- rate entity for a year of income -- 25%; or (b) otherwise -- 30%; if subsections (3) to (5) and section 23A do not apply to
-- the company." No year limits: s 23 has no table by year, so it answers for every year.
@export At what rate is my company's taxable income taxed, in percent (s 23(2))?
GIVEN `c` IS A Company @desc Your company's facts for the year of income
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `At what rate is my company taxed` IS
    CONSIDER `c`'s `kind`
    WHEN `an RSA provider, PDF, life insurance company, credit union or trustee` THEN `Not covered by this encoding`
    WHEN `an ordinary company` THEN
        IF `Is my company a base rate entity` `c` THEN Amount 25 ELSE Amount 30

§§ `s 23(6) -- the non-profit ceiling`

-- "The amount of tax payable by a company (before applying any rebate, credit or other tax offset ...) must not be greater than
-- 55% of the amount (if any) by which the taxable income of the company exceeds $416, if: (a) the company is a non-profit
-- company; and (b) the taxable income is not greater than: (i) if the company is a base rate entity for a year of income --
-- $762; or (ii) otherwise -- $915."
GIVEN `c` IS A Company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the non-profit ceiling applies` MEANS
        `Is my company a non-profit company` `c`
    AND (    (`Is my company a base rate entity` `c` AND `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST 762)
          OR ((NOT `Is my company a base rate entity` `c`) AND `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST 915))

@export How much tax must my company pay before offsets (s 23(2), (6))?
GIVEN `c` IS A Company @desc Your company's facts for the year of income
GIVETH AN Answer
DECIDE `How much tax must my company pay` IS
    CONSIDER `At what rate is my company taxed` `c`
    WHEN Amount `rate` THEN
        IF `c`'s `taxable income` AT MOST 0 THEN Amount 0
        ELSE IF `the non-profit ceiling applies` `c`
             THEN Amount (`the lesser of` (`c`'s `taxable income` TIMES `rate` DIVIDED BY 100)
                                          (`the slice` (`c`'s `taxable income`) 416 `no upper limit` TIMES 55 DIVIDED BY 100))
             ELSE Amount (`c`'s `taxable income` TIMES `rate` DIVIDED BY 100)
    OTHERWISE `Not covered by this encoding`
